    "description": "A scent that anchors the light when you feel unseen.</p> <p>There are moments when the world looks through you—when your presence is softened, your voice hushed, your radiance dimmed by self-doubt or silence.<br /> Meant to Be Seen is born from those moments. Not to mask them, but to transform them.</p> <p>It is a fragrance that acts as an anchor of light—a quiet yet powerful reminder that your essence deserves to be felt, noticed, remembered.</p> <p>Opening with the delicate brightness of bergamot and the tender grace of violet, the scent begins with a breath of clarity. At its heart, the rich creaminess of iris butter intertwines with moxalone and a soft animalic trace of civettone, creating a sensation of vulnerability refined into strength—delicate, yet unwavering.</p> <p>The base grounds this luminescence with unexpected warmth. Sesame and sandalwood brings a nutty, textured depth, while ambrettolide and akigalawood wrap the composition in a radiant, skin-like finish—soft, sensual, and lingering.</p> <p>Meant to Be Seen is not just a perfume—it is a declaration. For the quiet ones. For the daydreamers. For those whose glow has been dimmed but never lost. This is the scent that finds you in your stillness and reminds you:</p> <p>You were never meant to hide. You were always meant to be seen.",
